    "old": "      seq = line.seq;\n      if (bubbleLineOk(BUBBLE_TAB, line)) say(line.id, line.text);",
    "new": "      if (bubbleLineOk(BUBBLE_TAB, line)) { seq = line.seq; say(line.id, line.text); }",
    "equivalent": true,
    "why": "A refused line produces nothing either way - the watermark past it buys a walk, not a law. The only difference is that a session with one system notice in the log re-reads that one line every frame for the rest of its life, which is a cost no pin can see and none here pretends to. Kept as written because the cost is real and the shape ('read forward, once') is the one a later channel tab will inherit.",
